Context for the recall evaluation set (T107, plan 003 R5).

Why markers, not pinned event IDs: markers keep the corpus editable
without repinning; TestRecallDeterministic pins ID and rank stability
per corpus revision instead. Why a tool-output answer question: T112
(plan 004 O6) is unblocked only once the set can measure recall with
tool outputs excluded from the index; the unindex test proves it can.
Rationale lives in testdata/recall/README.md and NOTES.md.
